# Ebb — Cold Start

State lives in git and the work graph, so this works after any shutdown, reboot, or fresh clone. Nothing needs saving on the way out.

## Minimum viable fleet

Commander + one worker + one reviewer. Start there. It is a working loop, and it is what makes this installable rather than aspirational.

## 1. Commander

```bash
cd /path/to/project-root
claude
```

The folder's `CLAUDE.md` makes this session the commander. No launcher required.

> If you run your own agent harness, launch the commander with it instead — the folder context does the rest.

## 2. Seats

Per seat, in its own terminal:

```bash
export CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR="$HOME/.claude-seats/seat-worker-1"   # or seat-reviewer
cd /path/to/project-root
claude
```

Paste that seat's standing prompt from `fleet/SEATS.md`. The seat idles until the commander sends it work by name.

## 3. Wire discovery, then verify

Per-seat config directories isolate each seat's session registry, so the commander cannot message a seat until their registrations are shared. Run the procedure in `runbooks/SEAT_DISCOVERY.md`, then ask the commander to verify the fleet: it should list every seat and round-trip a message to each. A seat that does not answer gets relaunched.

## 4. Feed it

Speak backlog items to the commander in plain language. It files them as beads, the fleet claims them, the reviewer gates them with bench evidence, and merges land per this project's merge policy.

## Shutdown

Close the terminals in any order. In-flight work resumes from the graph.
